<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13304" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονίνᾰμαι</span></b> , 
			Med.
		, fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hom.
				</span></i>
			: 
				Ep.
			aor. 2 without augm. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονήμην, ἀπόνητο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hom.
				</span></i>
			; 2sg. opt. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόναιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.556
				</span></i>
			, 3pl.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποναίατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Cer.</u>
					132
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				211
			</span></i> (lyr.); inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόνασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.196
				</span></i>
			; part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονήμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					24.30
				</span></i>
			: later aor. I 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπωνάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Am.</u>
					52
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>in Alc.</u>
				p.89C.
			</span></i>:—<i>have the use</i> or <i>enjoyment of</i> a
			thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἧς ἥβης ἀπόνητο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.25
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶνδ᾽ ἀπόναιο</span>
			<i>mayest</i> thou <i>have joy of</i> them, ib.<i><span class="en">
				24.556
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμῆς ἀπονήμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδέ ποτ᾽ ἀγλαΐας ἀποναίατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					211
				</span></i>
			: without gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦγε μὲν οὐδ᾽
				ἀπόνητο</span> married her but <i>had</i> no <i>joy</i>
			[of it], <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.324
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρέψε μὲν οὐδ᾽ ἀπόνητο</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				17.293
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				16.120
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλιν κτίσας οὐκ ἀπόνητο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.168
				</span></i>
			.</div>
